      "writtenOn": "2018-08-06T18:34:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It can\u0027t be the same AndroidTest.xml because those describe how to run the test.\n\nI.E. for a device test: push the binary, execute the binary using device test class (Gtest.java).\nFor a host test: execute the binary using host test class (HostGtest.java)\n\n\nDan wanted to avoid a new implicit file check (i.e. DevicelessTest.xml) and instead suggested this new argument. My plan is for 99% of the host gtests configs to be autogenerated. But a dev might have a need to support a custom config here or there. Also it\u0027s worth noting that all cases today use the implicit AndroidTest.xml or autogenerate.\n\nI\u0027m not fully familiar with Android.bp but when I talked to Dan he suggested that there can be a sub-configuration for the device/host targets to handle when the dev wants to say \"use this file for the target and this other file for the host\".",
      "parentUuid": "1d701ec7_b2b69235",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 45
      },
